Z||000000||gtjeff||08-25-2001||01:38 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.bonforums.com/comp/camaro_next.htm" TARGET=_blank>www.bonforums.com/comp/camaro_next.htm</A> <P>This article states "BON has learned from a source at within the division that Pontiac is working on a high performance car to be built at Bowling Green on a different unidentified platform."<P>They then speculate that this will be a GTO.<BR>Why would a muscle car be built in a plant that specializes in sports cars? My feeling is this model if true is another sports car!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Pontiaddict||08-25-2001||11:37 PM||||I'd guess that Chevy doesn't want the Evoq built on a Corvette chassis and that they are going to build a custom chassis for Caddy and need another car to share with to justify the cost of building a seperate platform.<P>Just a guess and it's pure speculation.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fformula88||08-26-2001||12:30 PM||||I am glad to hear they are working on a high performance Pontiac.  They certainly need something after they kill off the Firebird.  It look sbad to me when GM's "sport/performance" division has NO sports cars.<P>I hope they can do it, but the Chevy boys were afraid of the Fiero eating into Vette sales... I am not sure they will like a high performance Pontiac.  Especially one built in Bowling Green!<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierosig2.JPG"> <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
