Z||000004||Formula88||08-26-2001||01:06 PM||||There has been speculation about the Grand Am taking over the performance banner for Pontiac after the demise of the Firebird.  Of course, this news comes from <A HREF="http://www.grandamgt.com" TARGET=_blank>www.grandamgt.com</A>  , so take that with a grain of salt.  However, the Grand Am SC/T concept car with a 262HP supercharged 3400 sure seems like a fun car.  I have a 99 Grand Am as my daily driver and it's a good platform to build on.  I just can see them giving the performance flagship duties to a front wheel drive car - I don't care how fast it is.  <P>Here's a couple pics of the SC/T roadster and it's engine...<P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SCT_Roadster_Stockcar-small.jpg">  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/3400SC_small.jpg">    <p>[This message has been edited by Formula88 (edited 08-26-2001).]||||reg||1
